   "id": "shabbat.51a.2",
   "daf": "51a",
   "sentenceId": 1,
   "he": "מַתְנִי׳ לֹא כִּסָּהוּ מִבְּעוֹד יוֹם — לֹא יְכַסֶּנּוּ מִשֶּׁתֶּחְשַׁךְ. כִּסָּהוּ וְנִתְגַּלָּה, מוּתָּר לְכַסּוֹתוֹ. מְמַלֵּא אֶת הַקִּיתוֹן וְנוֹתֵן לְתַחַת הַכַּר אוֹ תַּחַת הַכֶּסֶת.",
   "en": "«MISHNA:» If «one did not cover» a pot of cooked food on Shabbat eve «while it was still day, he may not cover it after dark.» However, if «one covered it» while it was still day «and it was uncovered» on Shabbat, «he is permitted to cover it» even on Shabbat. «One may fill a jug» with cold water on Shabbat «and place» it «beneath a pillow or a cushion» to prevent it from getting warm."
  }
 ],
